# MATSS — LLM credentials.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (which is gitignored — NEVER commit your real keys),
# then fill in the key for the provider you run with `--provider`.
#
#   python -m matss.app.runner --provider openrouter --days 2
#
# Each provider reads its specific variable first, then falls back to the generic
# API_KEY below — so you can either set the specific one, or just set API_KEY to
# the key for whichever single provider you use.

# --- OpenRouter (Google Gemma — the default reasoning model) ------------------
# Key looks like: sk-or-v1-...
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# --- OpenAI -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Key looks like: sk-proj-... or sk-...
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# --- Anthropic ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Key looks like: sk-ant-...
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Generic fallback ---------------------------------------------------------
# Used by whichever provider you select if its specific variable above is unset.
# Put here the key for the ONE provider you run. (The legacy code also used this
# name.) Make sure the key type matches your --provider:
#   --provider openrouter  -> an OpenRouter key (sk-or-v1-...)
#   --provider openai      -> an OpenAI key     (sk-proj-... / sk-...)
# API_KEY=
